# Worldgorger Dragon and Animate Dead, the loop of mandatory actions that is a draw (CR 104.4b, 732.4). Bot1 Entombs the
# Dragon on turn 1 and animates it on turn 3. The Dragon enters; its enters ability exiles Animate Dead and both Swamps
# (all other permanents Bot1 controls), so Animate Dead's leaves ability makes Bot1 sacrifice the Dragon, whose leaves
# ability returns the exiled cards, new objects (CR 400.7), the Swamps untapped. Animate Dead, put onto the battlefield
# without being cast, chooses what it enchants (CR 303.4f): a creature card in a graveyard, and the Dragon is the only
# one, so it enchants the Dragon without anyone choosing; its enters ability returns the Dragon, and round it goes. Each
# trigger has no target or one, the Dragon's two abilities never trigger together, and at every priority neither player
# can do anything but pass or tap a Swamp for mana (their hands are only basic lands; no spell is castable with a trigger
# on the stack), and tapping a land only fills a pool that buys nothing: no player can stop it. Both only pass, and once it
# has come round three times the game is a draw (docs/rules-exceptions.md, RX-4).

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Entomb
Animate Dead
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Worldgorger Dragon
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Entomb.Cast
Bot1.Search(Worldgorger Dragon)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Graveyard = Entomb; Worldgorger Dragon
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Animate Dead.Cast(Bot1.Graveyard.Worldgorger Dragon)

[Expect]
Result = Draw
DrawReason = MandatoryLoop
Turn = 3
Step = Main1
Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Hand = Swamp; Swamp; Swamp; Swamp
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Status = (absent)
Bot2.Status = (absent)
